---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About — AI Research">
  <article>
    <div class="kicker">About</div>
    <h1>A scientist interested in intelligent systems.</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      I am an Applied Scientist at Microsoft, where I work on large-scale AI
      systems spanning multimodal reasoning, foundation-model post-training,
      agentic simulation, and machine-learning infrastructure.
    </p>

    <p>
      Over the years, my work has moved from molecular and graph-based learning
      systems into increasingly general AI systems. That transition has made me
      interested not only in building capable models, but in understanding the
      scientific questions underneath them.
    </p>

    <p>
      I enjoy problems where research and engineering cannot be separated:
      designing experiments, understanding why a model behaves the way it does,
      building the infrastructure to test the hypothesis, and then turning the
      result into something that works at real scale.
    </p>

    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Scientific understanding over benchmark chasing.</li>
      <li>Research that survives contact with real systems.</li>
      <li>Efficient and accessible intelligence.</li>
      <li>Evaluation that reflects how models actually behave.</li>
      <li>Making advanced AI research more egalitarian and broadly accessible.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Outside the technical details</h2>
    <p>
      I am especially interested in the relationship between scientific
      progress, engineering constraints, and the institutions that determine
      who gets to participate in frontier AI research.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>